Funding-Text = {This work was supported by the IK Prize 2015, an annual award hosted by
   Tate Britain to support the development of an innovative project that
   uses technology to create new ways for the public to discover,
   experience and enjoy art from the Tate collection. Tate Sensorium was
   the winning project 2015 (http://tate.org.uk/ikprize), a multisensory
   display at Tate Britain (26/08/2015-04/10/2015) featuring four paintings
   from the Tate collection experienced through sound, smell, taste and
