Abstract = {This paper explores the valuation of Nature-based Solutions (NbS) and
   the critical considerations involved in their economic assessment. NbS
   leverage ecosystems to achieve goals such as biodiversity protection,
   with applications ranging from urban green spaces to large-scale forest
   conservation. This paper discusses the social and economic value of
   ecosystem services provided by NbS. Economic methods for valuing
   biodiversity, including Revealed Preference, Stated Preference, and
   Production Function methods, are examined, highlighting their critical
   aspects and the importance of integrating non-market values into policy
   decisions.},
